.TH SDL_TrayClickCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_TrayClickCallback \- A callback that is invoked when the tray icon is clicked.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef bool (SDLCALL *SDL_TrayClickCallback)(void *userdata, SDL_Tray *tray);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
an optional pointer to pass extra data to the callback when it will be invoked\[char46] May be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I tray
the tray that was clicked\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true to show the tray menu after the callback returns, false to skip showing the menu\[char46] This return value is only used for left and right click callbacks; other mouse events ignore the return value\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateTrayWithProperties (3)
